    "No dose, formulation, or food-effect information for the query, which could alter the impact of low intrinsic solubility.",
    "L1 F measurements are for other molecules with limited structural transferability to this large symmetric dimer."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L4 adds measured low aqueous solubility for structurally related pyrrolidine carbamate–imidazole compounds (M05 parent <0.1 mg/mL; phosphate prodrug 6.4 µg/mL) and for atazanavir (<1 µg/mL at pH≥4), coherently supporting poor absorption for the query. The L1 high-F contexts are direct but poorly transferable because the query is much larger, more lipophilic, and has higher TPSA. The unfavorable physicochemical prior is now supported by experimental solubility evidence, so the prediction is flipped to low with moderate confidence."
